        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(memory-wiki): reject malformed ChatGPT timestamps",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\nChatGPT imports accepted malformed Unix timestamp strings like scientific notation or trailing newlines, which could normalize bad source data into valid page timestamps.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\nTightened `isoFromUnix` to only accept finite numeric values or canonical decimal strings, and added a CLI regression test covering malformed ChatGPT timestamp inputs.\n\n## User Impact\nChatGPT imports now reject malformed timestamp text instead of silently accepting it. Valid imports are unchanged.\n\n## Evidence\n- GitHub Actions run `29620423390` (`checks-node-changed`) passed on current head `8413f4ab725937b981f6bdcf13addef43a141eeb`; the `extensions/memory-wiki/src/cli.test.ts` shard reports `19 passed`.\n- GitHub Actions run `29620423390` (`openclaw/ci-gate`) passed on the same head.\n- The passing `checks-node-changed` shard includes the malformed ChatGPT timestamp regression in `extensions/memory-wiki/src/cli.test.ts`.",
